 overview='Some time after the birth, a caravan from the East arrived in Jerusalem with one question: “Where is he that is born King of the Jews?” (Matthew 2:2). The travelers were Magi, priest-scholars with a seat at the Parthian court, and they had seen His star. Their question shook Herod, the king Rome had installed, and the whole city with him. Herod’s own scholars supplied the answer from Micah 5:2: Bethlehem. Then Herod questioned the Magi in private and sent them on with a request that sounded like worship and was really a trap. This lesson looks at who the Magi were, what the star may have been, and why one question frightened a king.',
